{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:17723218 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:17723218 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"17723218","source":"MED","pmid":"17723218","pmcid":"PMC2034442","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC2034442"]},"doi":"10.1016/j.immuni.2007.07.010","title":"Inflammation directs memory precursor and short-lived effector CD8(+) T cell fates via the graded expression of T-bet transcription factor.","authorString":"Joshi NS, Cui W, Chandele A, Lee HK, Urso DR, Hagman J, Gapin L, Kaech SM.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Joshi NS","lastName":"Joshi","firstName":"Nikhil S","initials":"NS","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7045-7837"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Immunobiology, Yale University School of Medicine, New Haven, CT 06520, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Cui W","lastName":"Cui","firstName":"Weiguo","initials":"W","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1562-9218"}},{"fullName":"Chandele A","lastName":"Chandele","firstName":"Anmol","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Lee HK","lastName":"Lee","firstName":"Heung Kyu","initials":"HK","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3977-1510"}},{"fullName":"Urso DR","lastName":"Urso","firstName":"David R","initials":"DR"},{"fullName":"Hagman J","lastName":"Hagman","firstName":"James","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5436-8455"}},{"fullName":"Gapin L","lastName":"Gapin","firstName":"Laurent","initials":"L"},{"fullName":"Kaech SM","lastName":"Kaech","firstName":"Susan M","initials":"SM"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3977-1510"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5436-8455"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7045-7837"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1562-9218"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","recommended_reviews","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"2","volume":"27","journalIssueId":1458986,"dateOfPublication":"2007 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2007,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Immunity","title":"Immunity","essn":"1097-4180","issn":"1074-7613","isoabbreviation":"Immunity","nlmid":"9432918"},"printPublicationDate":"2007-08-01"},"pubYear":"2007","pageInfo":"281-295","abstractText":"As acute infections resolve, effector CD8(+) T cells differentiate into interleukin-7 receptor(lo) (IL-7R(lo)) short-lived effector cells (SLECs) and IL-7R(hi) memory precursor effector cells (MPECs) capable of generating long-lived memory CD8(+) T cells. By using another SLEC marker, KLRG1, we found that KLRG1(hi) effector cells began appearing early during infection and were committed to downregulating IL-7R. Unlike IL-7R(hi) MPECs, KLRG1(hi) IL-7R(lo) SLECs relied on IL-15, but IL-15 could not sustain their long-term maintenance or homeostatic turnover. The decision between SLEC and MPEC fates was regulated by the amount of inflammatory cytokines (i.e., IL-12) present during T cell priming. According to the amount of inflammation, a gradient of T-bet was created in which high T-bet expression induced SLECs and low expression promoted MPECs. These results elucidate a mechanism by which the innate immune system sets the relative amounts of a lineage-determining transcription factor in activated CD8(+) T cells and, correspondingly, regulates their memory cell potential.","affiliation":"Department of Immunobiology, Yale University School of Medicine, New Haven, CT 06520, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIAID NIH HHS","acronym":"AI","grantId":"P01 AI022295","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIAID NIH HHS","acronym":"AI","grantId":"R01 AI057485","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIAID NIH